@page "/HowTo"


<div class="blurthing2">
            <h1 class="pageh1">HOW TO USE</h1>
            <br>
            <div class="navbar" style="font-size:14px; height:20px;">
	             CURRENCY EXCHANGE TOOL
            </div>
                <p style="padding:10px;">Enter in any value in one of the three boxes, calculations happen automatically in real time.
                <ul>
                <li>Red represents Roubles.</li>
                <li>Green represents Dollars.</li>
                <li>Blue represents Euros. </li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            <br>
            <div class="navbar" style="font-size:14px; height:20px;">
	              TAX CALCULATOR
            </div>
                <ol>
                <li>Select item to list.</li>
                <li>Select Vendor.</li>
                <li>Enter in the value of the buy back into the VENDOR BUY BACK box.</li>
                <li>Enter in the potential listing value in DESIRED LIST PRICE box.</li>
                <li>If listing more than one item, enter item quantity.
                    <div style="font-size:14px;padding:4px;">A: &nbsp; If selling items in bulk, check BULK SALE.</div>
                   <div style="font-size:14px;padding:4px; color: rgba(180,177,171,1.00);">NOTE: BULK SALE only appears in item quantities of 2 or more.</div></li>
                <li>If Level 3 Intelligence is unlocked in hideout, check the box.
                    <div style="font-size:14px;padding:4px;">A: &nbsp; Enter the level of your Hideout Management Skill</div>
                   <div style="font-size:14px;padding:4px; color: rgba(180,177,171,1.00);">NOTE: HIDEOUT MANAGEMENT (MGMT) level will appear only after LEVEL 3 INTEL is checked.</div></li>
                <li>(Optional) Enter in the competing market price for charting.</li>
                <li>(Optional) Enter in any crafting / material costs into INVESTMENT. This provides a more accurate REALIZED GAINS.</li>
                </ol>
            
             @*<div class="navbar" style="font-size:14px; height:20px;">
	             GLOSSARY
            </div>
                <p>
                    <ul style="list-style-type:none">
                        <li>BASE VALUE - The hidden value of an item in game, used in calculations for flea tax rate.</li>
                        <li>BREAK EVEN - The lowest list price to cover the loss of taxes paid for listing, resulting in zero or near zero profits.</li>
                        <li>LOWEST TAX % - The point along the algorithm in which the paid taxes for listing are the lowest.</li>
                        <li>MARGIN HIGH - The list price point before a sharp rise in slope, maximizing positive profits. Preventing net loss due to flea tax.</li>
                        <li>MARGIN LOW - The list price point before a sharp decline in slope. Prevents net loss on low price listings where profit margins are already slim.</li>
                        <li>VALUATION - An indicator of a buyer's market or a seller's market. Assitsts in determining selling or buying based off of Desired List Price and the Market Price.</li>
                        <li>FLEA REP GAIN - An indicator of Flea Reputation on a given listing. Indicator is blue when the 50,000 Rouble transaction met, white when building reputation before 1 point, and red when losing reputation from a listing.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <br>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: none;">
                        <li>EST. TOTAL - Estimated total of taxes to be paid. Will automatically update as values change.</li>
                        <li>PER ITEM - Tax paid per item.</li>
                        <li>STANDARD TAX - The default tax rate with no discounts.</li>
                        <li>DISCOUNT TAX - The taxes with all discounts applied.</li>
                        <li>DISCOUNT SAVINGS - The amount of taxes saved when discounts apply.</li>
                        <li>TAX % OF BASE - The percentage of taxes to be paid off of the BASE VALUE. This indicator assists in determining the value to tax ratio.</li>
                        <li>% PAID IN TAX - The percentage of taxes to be paid along the curve, representing LISTING PRICE and EST. TAXES.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <br>
                    <ul style="list-style-type:none">
                        <li>SALES GROSS - The gross income, unadjusted for any deficits or deductions.</li>
                        <li>SALES - TAX - The net income adjusted for tax, the value earned after a sale occurs.</li>
                        <li>REALIZED GAINS - Total profit when adjusted for taxes and INVESTMENTS are deducted. </li>
                    </ul>
                    <br>
                    <ul style="list-style-type:none">
                        <li>OVER VENDOR - Profit earned over selling to a vendor.</li>
                        <li>ITEM - TAX - Per item SALES - TAX.</li>
                        <li>REALIZED - Total per item profit adjusted for taxes and INVESTMENTS.</li> 
                    </ul>
               </p>*@

</div>
